# SupremeOS native-linux — Gateway environment.
#
# Every variable here has a DIRECT counterpart in infra/hub-compose/docker-compose.yml's
# `gateway` service block, in the same order, so the two deployments can be diffed side by
# side. The only substantive changes are Docker service DNS names (`postgres`, `nats`,
# `mqtt`, `homeassistant`, `commissioning`) becoming `127.0.0.1` (native processes on
# loopback, no container network) and volume paths becoming this deployment's own
# directories. Values install.sh cannot know ahead of time (passwords, secrets, the
# system's own domain) are substituted from the install-time answers; everything else is
# the exact same documented default as .env.example.
#
# Every value is double-quoted. Not cosmetic: `SUPREME_SYSTEM_NAME` can contain spaces
# (e.g. "Supreme Residence"), and an UNQUOTED value with a space breaks anything that
# treats this as a real shell environment file (confirmed directly — `source`-ing an
# earlier, unquoted render of this file failed with "Residence: command not found").
# systemd's own `EnvironmentFile=` parser accepts double-quoted values identically to a
# shell (systemd.exec(5)), so quoting costs nothing there and fixes a real footgun
# everywhere else this file gets read (manual debugging, a future script).
#
# Rendered to /etc/supremeos/gateway.env (mode 0640, owned root:supreme) by install.sh;
# loaded by systemd/supreme-gateway.service via EnvironmentFile=.

SUPREME_HOST="0.0.0.0"
SUPREME_PORT="8080"
SUPREME_BACKEND="___SUPREME_BACKEND___"
SUPREME_HA_URL="ws://127.0.0.1:8123/api/websocket"
SUPREME_HA_TOKEN="___SUPREME_HA_TOKEN___"
SUPREME_HA_ADMIN_USER="___SUPREME_HA_ADMIN_USER___"
SUPREME_HA_ADMIN_PASSWORD="___SUPREME_HA_ADMIN_PASSWORD___"
SUPREME_SECRETS_DIR="___SUPREME_SECRETS_DIR___"
SUPREME_SYSTEM_NAME="___SUPREME_SYSTEM_NAME___"
SUPREME_UNSPLASH_KEY="___SUPREME_UNSPLASH_KEY___"
SUPREME_TZ="___SUPREME_TZ___"
SUPREME_DEV_MODE="0"
SUPREME_SETUP_WIZARD="___SUPREME_SETUP_WIZARD___"
SUPREME_TOKEN_SECRET="___SUPREME_TOKEN_SECRET___"
DATABASE_URL="postgres://supreme:___POSTGRES_PASSWORD___@127.0.0.1:5432/supreme"
SUPREME_COMMISSIONING_URL="http://127.0.0.1:9100"
# The Docker deployment's `ai` (local LLM) and `appletv` (pyatv bridge) services are not
# yet part of this native deployment — see docs/architecture/Native-Linux-Deployment.md
# "Known scope gaps." Left empty (not pointed at a nonexistent localhost port) so the
# gateway falls back to its built-in planner / disables the Apple TV bridge honestly,
# exactly as it already does when SUPREME_AI_URL/SUPREME_APPLETV_URL are unset today.
SUPREME_AI_URL=""
SUPREME_APPLETV_URL=""
SUPREME_NATS_URL="nats://127.0.0.1:4222"
SUPREME_REDIS_URL="redis://127.0.0.1:6379"
SUPREME_OTEL_ENDPOINT=""
SUPREME_MQTT_URL="mqtt://127.0.0.1:1883"
SUPREME_MODBUS_HOST=""
SUPREME_MODBUS_PORT="502"
SUPREME_KNX_HOST=""
SUPREME_KNX_PORT="3671"
SUPREME_MATTER_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_MATTER_STORAGE_PATH="___SUPREME_DATA_DIR___/matter"
SUPREME_ZIGBEE_PORT=""
SUPREME_ZIGBEE_ADAPTER="zstack"
SUPREME_DALI_PORT=""
SUPREME_AVR_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_HEOS_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_YAMAHA_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_COOLMASTER_HOST=""
SUPREME_SIP_SERVER=""
SUPREME_WIIM_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_DEVIALET_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_SONOS_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_AJAX_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_SHELLY_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_AIRPLAY_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_APPLETV_ENABLED="0"
SUPREME_PUBLIC_BASE_URL="https://___SUPREME_DOMAIN___"
SUPREME_LUTRON_HOST=""
SUPREME_LUTRON_USERNAME="lutron"
SUPREME_LUTRON_PASSWORD="integration"
SUPREME_TUYA_ENABLED="0"
# go2rtc (camera streaming) is likewise not yet part of this native deployment — same
# honest-empty pattern as SUPREME_AI_URL/SUPREME_APPLETV_URL above.
SUPREME_STREAM_BASE_URL="https://___SUPREME_DOMAIN___/stream"
SUPREME_STREAM_ENGINE="go2rtc"
SUPREME_STREAM_API_URL=""
SUPREME_PUSH_RELAY_URL=""
SUPREME_PUSH_RELAY_TOKEN=""
SUPREME_RELAY_URL=""
SUPREME_RELAY_TOKEN=""
SUPREME_HUB_VERSION="___SUPREME_HUB_VERSION___"
SUPREME_LOG_LEVEL="___SUPREME_LOG_LEVEL___"
# § UI-triggered "Update now" (native-linux only — the hub-compose/Docker deployment's own
# gateway.env has no equivalent, so that deployment never sees this feature). Absolute path to
# THIS host's update.sh + the log file its systemd-run invocation appends to; see
# services/gateway/src/system-update-runner.ts and lib/common.sh's configure_update_sudoers().
SUPREME_UPDATE_SCRIPT="___SUPREME_UPDATE_SCRIPT___"
SUPREME_UPDATE_LOG="___SUPREME_UPDATE_LOG___"
NODE_ENV="production"
# § Real finding, verified by actually booting the gateway: `assertSecureConfig()`
# (services/gateway/src/config.ts) refuses to boot under NODE_ENV=production with an empty
# SUPREME_CORS_ORIGINS — "refusing to boot (production hardening): SUPREME_CORS_ORIGINS
# must be set in production". infra/hub-compose/docker-compose.yml sets the identical
# NODE_ENV=production default with the identical empty SUPREME_CORS_ORIGINS default, and
# its own .env.example never mentions this variable — the same fatal boot error is latent
# there too on a from-the-docs Docker bring-up. Fixed here (not silently left empty like
# Docker's own default) with the one origin this deployment's OWN Caddyfile actually serves
# the web UI from — same-origin by design, so this is not a guess.
SUPREME_CORS_ORIGINS="https://___SUPREME_DOMAIN___"
SUPREME_RATE_MAX="1000"
SUPREME_AUTH_RATE_MAX="20"
